Ours, for the Linux shader-check job only (never part of the Turnip that ships): Mesa's no-op drm-shim for msm gets an
entry for the Adreno 840 as iceland reports it (chip id 0x44050a31), so Turnip can be opened on a Linux runner as that
GPU (FD_GPU_ID=840) and its ir3 compiler run over SPIR-V with no hardware. Mesa 85fda3b's device table already matches
the chip id (its 0xffff44050A31 entry). MIT, as the file.

--- a/src/freedreno/drm-shim/freedreno_noop.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/drm-shim/freedreno_noop.c
@@ -318,6 +318,13 @@
       .chip_id = 0x44050000,
       .gmem_size = 12 * 1024 * 1024,
    },
+   {
+      /* iceland (OnePlus Pad 4, SM8850): the chip id the tablet's GPU reports. The GMEM size is the 830 entry's, not a
+       * measured one; nothing the shader-check job does depends on it (no rendering). */
+      .gpu_id = 840,
+      .chip_id = 0x44050a31,
+      .gmem_size = 12 * 1024 * 1024,
+   },
 };
 
 static void
